{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"Could one be found like this\"</b> is because he was a Hebrew, and they are an abomination to the Egyptians — they do not eat from their contact and do not associate with them, for they are impure to them. Therefore he did not wish to appoint him as second-in-command without their consent, and therefore he said to them that they would not find an Egyptian like him, for the spirit of Elohim is in him. And after they acknowledged this, he said to Joseph, \"After Elohim has made known to you all this\" — because since the interpretation was good and correct in the eyes of Pharaoh and in the eyes of his servants, it was in their eyes as though everything had already come about just as he interpreted for them. And it is possible that \"all this\" also alludes to what the chief butler had told him, as in (Genesis 29:13) \"and he told Laban all these things\" — the blessings mentioned earlier. He said: after Elohim has made known to you this great wisdom to interpret all the obscure and sealed dreams, and not a thing shall fall from all your words — there is none discerning and wise in any matter like you, and you are worthy to wield dominion and royalty and to be a second-in-command to me."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:18.114744622Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}